{%- comment -%}
  The design taxonomy.

  Shopify has no notion of a "design", let alone a family of designs, so the
  counter's own is built from two native pieces and nothing else:

    a design   a collection whose handle starts with the design prefix.
               Collections are the right carrier: a real URL, real product
               membership, pagination and native filtering come free.

    a family   the collection metafield `custom.design_family` — Florals,
               Geometrics, Block prints, whatever the counter calls them.
               Comma separated for a design that sits in more than one, or a
               list metafield, which arrives already split.

  Echoes the distinct families across every design that has cloth under it, as
  `slug|Name||slug|Name`. A family with nothing sellable in it is never
  emitted, so the book cannot offer a door that opens onto an empty room.

  Usage: {% render 'design-families' %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign prefix = settings.design_collection_prefix | default: 'design-'
  assign families = ''

  for collection in collections
    unless collection.handle contains prefix
      continue
    endunless
    if collection.products_count == 0
      continue
    endif

    assign raw = collection.metafields.custom.design_family.value
    if raw == blank
      continue
    endif

    # a list metafield arrives as an array, a text one as a string; join
    # leaves the string alone and flattens the list, so both read alike
    assign joined = raw | join: ','
    assign parts = joined | split: ','

    for part in parts
      assign name = part | strip
      if name == blank
        continue
      endif
      assign slug = name | handle
      assign probe = '|' | append: slug | append: '|'
      assign seen = '|' | append: families | append: '|'
      unless seen contains probe
        assign families = families | append: slug | append: '|' | append: name | append: '||'
      endunless
    endfor
  endfor

  echo families
-%}
